mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Local Services Marketplace — Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis canister backs a local services marketplace. Service providers (tutors, cleaners, handymen, gardeners) are listed with a profile, and customers browse, filter, review, and request bookings from them. Categories group providers, reviews carry star ratings and written feedback, and booking requests let a customer ask a provider for a date and time; the provider (or an admin) accepts or declines.\n\nAll content is manageable from within the app by an admin: providers, categories, and reviews can be created, edited, and removed, and sample content can be seeded once. A signed-in user may also create and manage their own single provider profile.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\nSign-in uses Internet Identity. The frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent that already holds the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\nRegistration is required before any role-guarded call. A caller registers by calling `_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in caller; the first caller to initialize becomes the admin, and every subsequent caller becomes a regular user. A caller that never signed in through this app's frontend is unregistered even if it belongs to the app's owner, and a principal derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered. An anonymous caller on a guarded endpoint fails the role check and traps with the endpoint's message, such as `Unauthorized: Only admins can create providers` or `Unauthorized: Only signed-in users can add a review`; a signed-in but unregistered caller traps with `User is not registered`.\n\n## Authorization\n\n- **Anonymous / unregistered**: may read the public catalogue — `listProviders`, `getProvider`, `listCategories`, `listReviewsForProvider`, `listProviderBookings` — and call `schema` / `execute` for entities exposed `#public_`.\n- **Signed-in user**: may create and manage their own provider profile (`getMyProvider`, `createMyProvider`, `updateMyProvider`, `deleteMyProvider`); may add, edit, and delete their own reviews; may create booking requests; and may list their own bookings (`listMyBookings`).\n- **Admin**: may create, update, and delete any provider, category, and review; may accept or decline booking requests; may seed sample data.\n\n## Methods\n\n### Providers\n- `listProviders(filter : ProviderFilter) : [ProviderView]` — query. Filter by `categoryId`, `location` (case-insensitive substring), and `search` (case-insensitive substring over name and description). Each view carries `averageRating` and `reviewCount`.\n- `getProvider(id : ProviderId) : ?ProviderView` — query.\n- `getMyProvider() : ?ProviderView` — query; signed-in only. Returns the caller's own provider profile, or `null` if the caller has none.\n- `createMyProvider(input : ProviderInput) : ProviderView` — signed-in only. Creates a provider profile owned by the caller; traps with `You already have a provider profile` if the caller already has one.\n- `updateMyProvider(input : ProviderInput) : ?ProviderView` — signed-in only. Updates the caller's own provider profile; traps with `You do not have a provider profile` if the caller has none.\n- `deleteMyProvider() : Bool` — signed-in only. Deletes the caller's own provider profile; traps with `You do not have a provider profile` if the caller has none.\n- `createProvider(input : ProviderInput) : ProviderView` — admin only.\n- `updateProvider(id : ProviderId, input : ProviderInput) : ?ProviderView` — admin only; returns `null` if the provider does not exist.\n- `deleteProvider(id : ProviderId) : Bool` — admin only; `false` if not found.\n\n### Categories\n- `listCategories() : [Category]` — query.\n- `createCategory(name : Text) : Category` — admin only.\n- `updateCategory(id : CategoryId, name : Text) : ?Category` — admin only.\n- `deleteCategory(id : CategoryId) : Bool` — admin only.\n\n### Reviews\n- `listReviewsForProvider(providerId : ProviderId) : [Review]` — query.\n- `addReview(input : ReviewInput) : Review` — signed-in only. `rating` must be 1–5; a caller may review a given provider only once.\n- `updateReview(id : ReviewId, rating : Nat, text : Text) : ?Review` — signed-in only; the author or an admin.\n- `deleteReview(id : ReviewId) : Bool` — signed-in only; the author or an admin.\n\n### Bookings\n- `createBooking(input : BookingInput) : BookingRequest` — signed-in only. The new request starts `#pending`.\n- `listMyBookings() : [BookingRequest]` — query; signed-in only, returns the caller's own requests.\n- `listProviderBookings(providerId : ProviderId) : [BookingRequest]` — query; all requests for a provider.\n- `acceptBooking(id : BookingId) : ?BookingRequest` — admin only.\n- `declineBooking(id : BookingId) : ?BookingRequest` — admin only.\n\n### Seeding\n- `seedSampleData() : ()` — admin only; seeds example categories, providers, and reviews once. A second call is a no-op.\n\n### Data intelligence (OQL)\n- `schema() : Text` — query; JSON schema of the queryable entities.\n- `execute(qJson : Text) : Result` — query; runs a JSON query against the entities.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- `Timestamp` is `Int` nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (UTC).\n- `hourlyRate` is a whole-number amount in the app's currency unit.\n- `rating` is an integer from 1 to 5.\n- `averageRating` is a `Float`; `0.0` when a provider has no reviews.\n- `photo` is an optional object-storage `ExternalBlob` reference (a UTF-8 `!caf!sha256:...` string), or `null`.\n- `owner` is the `Principal` that owns a provider profile: the caller for `createMyProvider`, or the admin caller for `createProvider`.\n- `BookingStatus` is the variant `#pending`, `#accepted`, or `#declined`.\n- `requestedDate` and `requestedTime` are free-form text supplied by the customer.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\nA booking request moves `#pending` → `#accepted` or `#declined` exactly once, when an admin responds. Poll `listMyBookings` (customer) or `listProviderBookings` (provider) to observe the change; there is no push notification. A booking that has been accepted or declined is not re-opened by this API.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `createProvider`, `createMyProvider`, `createCategory`, `addReview`, and `createBooking` are **not** idempotent: each successful call allocates a new id, so retrying after an ambiguous failure can create a duplicate. Read back with the corresponding list/get call before retrying.\n- `updateProvider`, `updateMyProvider`, `updateCategory`, `updateReview`, `acceptBooking`, and `declineBooking` are idempotent for a given id and payload.\n- `deleteProvider`, `deleteMyProvider`, `deleteCategory`, and `deleteReview` return `false` when the record is already gone, so a retry is safe.\n- `seedSampleData` is guarded by a one-time flag and is safe to retry.\n\n## Errors, traps, and gotchas\n\n- Authorization failures trap with a message beginning `Unauthorized:`.\n- `addReview` and `updateReview` trap when `rating` is outside 1–5, and `addReview` traps when the caller has already reviewed that provider.\n- `updateReview` and `deleteReview` trap when the review id does not exist.\n- `createMyProvider` traps when the caller already has a profile; `updateMyProvider` and `deleteMyProvider` trap when the caller has none.\n- `updateProvider`, `updateCategory`, `updateReview`, `acceptBooking`, and `declineBooking` return `null` (rather than trapping) when the target id does not exist.\n- `listProviderBookings` is public and returns every request for a provider, including the customer principal and message; treat it as non-private data.\n- OQL `execute` traps with `OQL: invalid query — ...` on malformed JSON."
  };
};
